{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00092",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.89,
      "end_seconds": 4.65,
      "duration_seconds": 3.76,
      "text": "Good morning. I hope the wait wasn't too long."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 6.28,
      "end_seconds": 7.4,
      "duration_seconds": 1.12,
      "text": "Good afternoon."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 9.4,
      "end_seconds": 11.78,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "So, what's been going on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 13.08,
      "end_seconds": 30.58,
      "duration_seconds": 17.5,
      "text": "I've been sweating, and I wanted to get it checked. It's a relief to finally sit down and talk about it. Well, I did have a headache afterwards at one point, but that's gone now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 32.53,
      "end_seconds": 36.78,
      "duration_seconds": 4.25,
      "text": "Right, have you been sweating at any time before this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 38.42,
      "end_seconds": 44.36,
      "duration_seconds": 5.94,
      "text": "I had a similar thing last winter. It went away."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 46.16,
      "end_seconds": 51.08,
      "duration_seconds": 4.92,
      "text": "Let me check a few things. Any vomiting, confusion or seizure?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 52.92,
      "end_seconds": 59.42,
      "duration_seconds": 6.5,
      "text": "Um, uh, no vomiting, confusion or seizure, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 60.11,
      "end_seconds": 64.17,
      "duration_seconds": 4.06,
      "text": "A few quick ones: weight loss or chest pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 66.15,
      "end_seconds": 69.17,
      "duration_seconds": 3.02,
      "text": "Oh, no, none of those."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 70.89,
      "end_seconds": 73.97,
      "duration_seconds": 3.08,
      "text": "How are your joints, any aches elsewhere?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 75.76,
      "end_seconds": 78.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.5,
      "text": "No, joints are fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 82.13,
      "end_seconds": 86.14,
      "duration_seconds": 4.01,
      "text": "Any change in your bowel habit or your stomach generally?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 90.77,
      "end_seconds": 93.93,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "No, that side's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 95.25,
      "end_seconds": 99.95,
      "duration_seconds": 4.7,
      "text": "Any medication at the moment, including things from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 101.29,
      "end_seconds": 107.49,
      "duration_seconds": 6.2,
      "text": "I take something called glyc... Glycomet, 500 milligrams, maybe, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 109.14,
      "end_seconds": 113.9,
      "duration_seconds": 4.76,
      "text": "Do you have the packet or the prescription with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 115.1,
      "end_seconds": 119.48,
      "duration_seconds": 4.38,
      "text": "Not with me. I'll bring it next time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 137.01,
      "end_seconds": 139.77,
      "duration_seconds": 2.76,
      "text": "Any diagnoses you've been given before?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 141.78,
      "end_seconds": 144.74,
      "duration_seconds": 2.96,
      "text": "I've, I've had diabetes, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 146.51,
      "end_seconds": 151.05,
      "duration_seconds": 4.54,
      "text": "Okay, I can see diabetes in your file as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 168.81,
      "end_seconds": 171.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.67,
      "text": "Have you had any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 176.4,
      "end_seconds": 178.14,
      "duration_seconds": 1.74,
      "text": "No operations, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 179.91,
      "end_seconds": 181.54,
      "duration_seconds": 1.63,
      "text": "Do you drink alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 182.38,
      "end_seconds": 187.81,
      "duration_seconds": 5.43,
      "text": "I have a couple of drinks on the weekend."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 189.31,
      "end_seconds": 190.54,
      "duration_seconds": 1.23,
      "text": "Do you smoke?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 192.13,
      "end_seconds": 193.7,
      "duration_seconds": 1.57,
      "text": "I've never smoked."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 195.09,
      "end_seconds": 197.29,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "Do you get any exercise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 198.27,
      "end_seconds": 203.65,
      "duration_seconds": 5.38,
      "text": "I walk for about half an hour most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 208.9,
      "end_seconds": 211.3,
      "duration_seconds": 2.4,
      "text": "How do you eat, generally?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 212.1,
      "end_seconds": 214.97,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "I skip breakfast most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 216.67,
      "end_seconds": 219.43,
      "duration_seconds": 2.76,
      "text": "Any allergies I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 220.27,
      "end_seconds": 224.04,
      "duration_seconds": 3.77,
      "text": "No, none that I know of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 225.69,
      "end_seconds": 228.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "I'll check your pressure and pulse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 240.15,
      "end_seconds": 241.09,
      "duration_seconds": 0.94,
      "text": "One second..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 252.85,
      "end_seconds": 267.61,
      "duration_seconds": 14.76,
      "text": "Okay: oxygen saturation is 99 percent, pulse is 82 beats a minute, height 150 centimetres, pressure 122 over 73, temp 36.9 degrees, BMI works out to 32.9, weight 74 kilos."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 268.45,
      "end_seconds": 270.14,
      "duration_seconds": 1.69,
      "text": "Is that okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 271.5,
      "end_seconds": 274.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "That's fine, we'll come to it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 276.18,
      "end_seconds": 278.63,
      "duration_seconds": 2.45,
      "text": "Okay, a quick examination now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 280.03,
      "end_seconds": 282.34,
      "duration_seconds": 2.31,
      "text": "Hold that position for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 291.31,
      "end_seconds": 294.92,
      "duration_seconds": 3.61,
      "text": "Pulse is normal and there's no tremor right now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 312.28,
      "end_seconds": 313.32,
      "duration_seconds": 1.04,
      "text": "Go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 317.09,
      "end_seconds": 327.68,
      "duration_seconds": 10.59,
      "text": "So, thanks for that. Right, here's what I'm thinking. The most likely explanation is low sugar episodes related to diabetes medication."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 329.62,
      "end_seconds": 333.26,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "Is this something I'll have for good?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 334.64,
      "end_seconds": 363.78,
      "duration_seconds": 29.14,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like low sugar episodes related to diabetes medication, but I'd like to confirm. I'll request a blood sugar test, it'll help with hypoglycaemia. I'll request an HbA1c, it'll help with diabetes control. Always keep glucose tablets or a sweet in your bag, and don't skip meals if you've taken your sugar tablet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 364.9,
      "end_seconds": 374.37,
      "duration_seconds": 9.47,
      "text": "And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 375.94,
      "end_seconds": 377.52,
      "duration_seconds": 1.58,
      "text": "Okay, I'll remember."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 378.07,
      "end_seconds": 386.44,
      "duration_seconds": 8.37,
      "text": "One warning sign to remember: you black out or can't wake up properly after an episode. In that case don't wait."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 387.55,
      "end_seconds": 390.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.64,
      "text": "Yes, I'll watch for that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 390.72,
      "end_seconds": 398.65,
      "duration_seconds": 7.93,
      "text": "Let's review you after the results are back. Alright, take care, and call us if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 400.39,
      "end_seconds": 402.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "Thank you for your time."
    }
  ]
}